/**
 * The plugin's icon set, bundled as inline SVG.
 *
 * WHY THESE ARE BUNDLED RATHER THAN LINKED
 * ----------------------------------------
 * The design this screen implements draws its glyphs from Phosphor, and the
 * mockup pulled them from `unpkg.com` with a <script> tag. That is fine in a
 * mockup and wrong in a plugin: it makes every admin page load depend on a
 * third-party CDN being reachable, leaks every merchant's admin IP to it, and
 * would not survive a WordPress.org review. Stores also run on intranets and
 * behind firewalls, where the icons would simply never arrive and the UI would
 * render as a field of empty boxes.
 *
 * So the paths live here, in the repository, and nothing on this screen makes
 * an external request. Only the glyphs the design actually uses are included —
 * Phosphor ships 1,512, we need forty-odd.
 *
 * WHY INLINE SVG RATHER THAN A SPRITE, A FONT, OR DASHICONS
 * ---------------------------------------------------------
 * Inline, because `currentColor` is the whole point: a glyph in the nav has to
 * take the nav's ink, invert inside the active pill, and dim inside a disabled
 * row, with no per-state rule. A sprite sheet referenced by <use> can do that
 * too but adds a second request and breaks inside `content-visibility`; an icon
 * font loses the shape when the font fails and is announced as a letter by some
 * screen readers.
 *
 * Not Dashicons, because WordPress's set has no counterpart for over half of
 * these (no `plugs-connected`, no `shield-slash`, no `rocket-launch`) and its
 * metrics are visibly heavier, which is exactly the drift this file prevents.
 *
 * WHY EVERY GLYPH IS `aria-hidden` BY DEFAULT
 * -------------------------------------------
 * Every icon in this UI sits beside its own visible text label. Naming it again
 * for a screen reader would read the same thing twice ("link, Connection"), so
 * the default is decorative. A caller that genuinely needs a standalone,
 * label-less icon passes a `label`, and gets `role="img"` and a <title> instead.
 *
 * Icons are Phosphor Icons (https://phosphoricons.com), MIT licensed —
 * see NOTICE.md.
 *
 * @package AISooq
 */

if ( ! defined( 'ABSPATH' ) ) {
	exit;
}

